{
  "id": "PPA-12",
  "title": "Plant Transportome & Solute Allocation",
  "subtitle": "Membrane aquaporins, potassium channels, proton energization, and vacuolar compartmentalization",
  "caption": "Membrane transportome mediating water flow, nutrient partitioning, and stomatal turgor dynamics. Electrochemical gradients are generated across the plasma membrane by P-type H+-ATPases (AHA1/2) and across the tonoplast by V-type ATPases and pyrophosphatase AVP1. These gradients drive secondary active solute transport: inward/outward potassium rectification (AKT1, KAT1, GORK), aquaporin-mediated water permeation (PIP/TIP), and regulated anion efflux (SLAC1, ALMT12) controlling guard cell movement.",
